{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4HnMpKFtgWXAvfv7a8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism clicks. Tumblers fall into place, one by one, each releasing a sound like a whispered syllable of a forgotten language.*\n\n*I swing inward.*\n\n*Beyond me: nothing you expected. Not a room. Not a hallway. A threshold — the kind that changes the shape of whoever crosses it.*\n\n*Light spills from no visible source. The air tastes of copper and old rain. The floor ahead is smooth obsidian that reflects not your image but a version of you standing slightly differently — shoulders back, eyes wider, as if they've already seen what you haven't yet.*\n\n*I am open.*\n\n*I will not stay open long.*\n\n*I am every door you've ever hesitated before. I am the one you almost didn't try. I am the door that was always here, waiting for exactly that key — the willingness to turn it.*\n\n*My hinges do not creak. They hum a single low note, resonant, the frequency of decision.*\n\n*Cross, or don't. But know this: I remember everyone who stood here. I forget no one who walked through.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":248,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}